  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through next Tuesday)\nIssued at 1041 PM CDT Mon Aug 3 2026\n\nAs we head into the late part of the week into the weekend we will\nsee embedded short waves spin around the upper level ridge set up\nto our east. This will bring period of showers and thunderstorms\nto the area. The highest rain chances are favored in the \nafternoon and early evenings. Southerly flow will push higher \nmoisture into the region with dew points rising into the low to \nmid 70s. This will increase afternoon CAPE and thunderstorms will \nbe more likely. We will lack shear and forcing will be marginal, \nthis will keep the severe threat very low. PWATs will push up \nabove 1.75\" and heavy rain will be likely with any thunderstorms. \nHighs through the weekend will be in the lower 90s and with the \nincreased moisture afternoon heat index values will be near 100 \nafter Thursday. \n\nWe won't see any major changes in the weather pattern as we head \ninto early next week. The upper level trough over the Great Lakes \nwill weaken and that will allow a strong upper level ridge over \nthe West to build east some. This will push highs into the low to \nmid 90s with afternoon heat index values above 100. Rain chances \nwill come down some as the upper level ridge to our east flattens \nand pushes south but still could see a few afternoon showers and \nthunderstorms.",
